<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Assassin Role Play</h1>
<p>Assassins deal in death. How they deal with it is as varied as the individuals. The best training school is in the city of Khorsabad which is a desert area with harsh living conditions. Assassins from all over Valhalla study there. Assassins do not study the divine paths. With exception of the Ranger guild, there is no guild with divine magics that will allow them admittance. It is believed they have an agreement with the Sorcerers of Midgaard due to some service performed in the past. Below are some tips, ideas and suggestions on how to play an assassin. Feel free to send in any others with the <a cmd='#'>idea</a> command. Who knows you may see it here!
</p>
<ul><li>Assassins work for various people from governments, religious orders, individuals and rebel groups. Many are freelancers who will work for anyone who pays them.</li>
<li>Assassins who renege on contracts tend to find little work and sometimes find they are the work for others.</li>
<li>It is rumored there is a secret organization of assassins in Khorsabad that will work for anyone for the right price.</li>
<li>An assassin may be a bounty hunter; not all bounty hunters are assassins, and many hate assassins.</li>
<li>Assassins are NOT thieves usually, but frequently employ them to get to their targets or to gather information about them. Woe to the thief that crosses an assassin's path when working, though.</li>
<li>Most assassins are conscientious about their contracts and retainers. In other words they stay bought until they have completed the task or time period for which they have been paid.</li>
<li>Assassins tend to be paranoid. They watch constantly and change routes frequently.</li>
<li>It is rumored the Midgaard Sorcerers are allied with and protect Assassins.</li>
<li>Some religious orders have been known to recruit assassins and promote them up the ranks of the Church.</li>
<li>Independent Assassins tend to be loners. They work alone and have few personal ties. They work for money not for politics or personal reasons.</li>
<li>Assassins retained by a government or noble may or may not be loyal.</li>
<li>Assassins retained by a religious order tend to be fanatics.</li>
<li>Assassins are pragmatic about death. They know their own may be bought at any time by anyone with a grudge.</li>
<li>Some Assassins REALLY enjoy their work, for others it is just a business.</li></ul>
